q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 34.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 15 TL (Hardware World sells hardware and construction materials. Its activities involve products, suppliers,) Tj T* (employees, customers, sales, procurement and payroll. When these records are kept separately, staff) Tj T* (may repeat information, lose transaction details or struggle to determine the available stock.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 54 610.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 49.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 15 TL (A sale must reduce stock and preserve the price charged. A delivery must increase stock. Payroll must) Tj T* (record gross pay, deductions and net pay. Managers need a common view of sales and payroll) Tj T* (movements. The database must connect these processes and prevent incomplete transactions from) Tj T* (leaving contradictory records.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 54 570.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 19.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 15 TL (The problem is therefore to develop a simple, connected system that stores business records reliably,) Tj T* (controls access and produces useful records for daily operations and management.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 54 543.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 5 Tm /F2 12 Tf 17 TL (Why we chose Hardware World) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 54 476.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 49.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 15 TL (The hardware retail business provides clear examples of database concepts. Categories and products) Tj T* (illustrate one-to-many relationships. Suppliers and products illustrate many-to-many relationships.) Tj T* (Employees and their supervisors illustrate a recursive relationship. Employee job types illustrate) Tj T* (specialization. Sales and payroll illustrate transactions and triggers.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 54 436.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 19.5 Tm /F1 10.5 Tf 15 TL (The system also solves a practical operational problem: a user can record a sale, see the remaining) Tj T* (stock, obtain a receipt and back up the resulting records through one application.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
